        }
      ],
      "message": "silentpayments: document recipient correctness requirement for sender\n\nBackground:\nAn adversary can create an address reusing another owner's scan public\nkey. If such an address is batched together with that owner's address,\nthe owner's output may be ordered after the adversary's and is then not\nfound by the BIP352 scanning algorithm.\n\nThanks to l0rinc for first finding this issue (PRed in Bitcoin Red\nTeam's bitcoin-security-council/secp256k1 repository on Sep. 19th).\nSimilar vulnerability reports were later submitted by the Anthropic OSS\nscanner (ANT-2026-X2ZAAB2N, Oct. 16th) and Project Loupe (Oct. 29th).",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Sebastian Falbesoner",
        "email": "sebastian.falbesoner@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-05T13:08:35Z"
